sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 4 + R1-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs). instance.create reuses this workflow for development Processes.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: process:create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: process:create queue<br/>--node=7 --command=… --start
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit process:create queue --node=7 --command=/usr/bin/php --command=artisan --command=queue:work --restart=on-failure --start`
  %%> - syntax: `process:create <name> (--instance=ID-or-domain | --node=ID-or-name | --project=ID --for=production) [options]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Process name and its owner: an Instance, a Node, or a Project definition
  %%> - the runtime (`systemd` or `docker`), command, image, environment, ports, volumes and restart policy
  %%> - `--start` to start it after it installs
  %%> Not handled here:
  %%> - a Project definition with `--for=production` is recorded only; it starts no run (R1)
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 418: pending · #5130
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the owner's Node
  %%> - the name is free for this owner
  %%> - a `--user` account exists on the Node
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Process 418 recorded with its definition, status pending
  %%> - the unit or container rendered; secret environment values pushed to the vault key `process-create-operation-5130`
  %%> - task #5130 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: process.create
  %%> - the rendered unit, or the container definition without its environment values
  %%> - the desired state, mounts and a retired name when the runtime or name changed
  %%> - vault key names for the environment, never the values
  %%> - the Node's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5130
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Check the account<br/>getent passwd orbit
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the account the Process runs as, and its home directory
  SW->>SW: Resolve check assets<br/>@nckrtl/process-command-assets
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - validates the intent and finds the shipped Process scripts on Node 209
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the scripts check ownership: they act only on the unit or container marked with Process 417
  SW->>N: Make the asset directory<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · mkdir
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - makes a private directory for this run on the Node, under `/tmp`
  SW->>N: Copy check assets<br/>@swamp/ssh copy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - copies the shipped scripts into that directory
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches the Node over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior, the `swamp` role SSH identity and the Node's pinned host keys
  SW->>N: Write the intent file<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file · 0600
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the public intent into the run directory for the scripts
  SW->>N: Inspect the Process<br/>inspect.py
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads whether the unit or container exists, its state and spec
  SW->>SW: Read the observation<br/>@nckrtl/process-command-assets
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - turns the inspection into fields later steps check
  opt production release, running
    SW->>N: Check the release<br/>check_release.py
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks that the admitted release directory exists
  end
  SW->>N: Check required mounts<br/>test -e <path>
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks each required mount path once; a systemd Process only
  opt runtime or name changed
    SW->>SW: Remove the retired unit<br/>child operation-process-destroy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the unit or container under its old name
  end
  alt systemd
    SW->>N: Write the environment<br/>lifecycle_environment.py · stdin
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the EnvironmentFile, root-owned 0600, from the vault value on stdin
    %%> Skipped:
    %%> - when the Process has no environment values
    SW->>N: Write the unit<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the rendered unit to `/etc/systemd/system`
    SW->>N: Reload systemd<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/exec
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs `systemctl daemon-reload`
    opt Vite dev Process
      SW->>N: Publish the dev route<br/>child operation-process-vite
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - suspends traffic, writes the Vite environment file and publishes Caddy for the Route
    end
    SW->>N: Stop a transitioning unit<br/>systemctl stop
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stops a unit that is still starting or stopping when the desired state is stopped
    SW->>N: Apply the unit state<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - enables and starts the unit when the desired state is running, unless it starts on demand; else disables and stops it
    SW->>N: Restart if changed<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd restart
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - restarts a running unit whose unit file changed
  else docker
    SW->>N: Pull the image<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/exec · docker pull
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - pulls the image unless it is already present
    SW->>N: Stop the old container<br/>control.py stop
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stops the owned container when its spec changed
    SW->>N: Remove the old container<br/>remove_container.py
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes that container; volumes stay
    SW->>N: Create the container<br/>lifecycle_container.py · stdin
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - creates the container; environment values come from the vault on stdin, never as arguments
    SW->>N: Create container, no env<br/>lifecycle_container.py
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the same, for a container without environment values
    SW->>N: Apply the container state<br/>docker container start|stop
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts or stops the container to match the desired state
  end
  SW->>N: Verify it runs<br/>verify.py
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks once that the unit or container has the desired state
  %%> Result:
  %%> - this step's output is the projected result
  opt Vite dev Process, running
    SW->>N: Check the listener<br/>lifecycle_listener.py
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks once that the Vite port listener belongs to this Process
    SW->>N: Prepare the awake marker<br/>mkdir <marker directory>
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - makes the hibernation marker directory
    SW->>N: Mark it awake<br/>touch <awake marker>
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - marks the Instance awake, so its Route serves traffic
  end
  SW->>N: Clean up<br/>remove the run directory
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the run directory after a successful run
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - the directory stays, so a resumed run can reuse the scripts
  SW->>SW: Report the result<br/>command/shell
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - prints the verified state as the run result
  alt Process running
    N-->>SW: active (running)
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Process has its desired state
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the result step once; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>Process 418: active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 becomes active with its desired state
    %%> - task #5130 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, a refusal such as `process.name_collision`, or the state does not match
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the Process failed<br/>task failed · rerun converges
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 is marked failed with the error code
    %%> - work done on the Node stays; a new `process:update` or create converges
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5130
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
